WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.536
-Our first guest tonight
is a very funny actress

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.705
you know from movies
such as "The Other Woman,"

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.140
"This is 40," and "Blockers."

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.607
She's currently starring
in "The Bubble,"

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.009
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.445
Please welcome back to the show
our friend Leslie Mann,

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.546
everybody.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.449
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:23.022
♪♪

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:29.595
♪♪

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:30.929
Hi!
-Hi!

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:33.666
-So lovely to see you!
-Yeah, it's been a long time.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.901
-it has been a long time.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.236
It is lovely
having you here in person.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.304
And I think, since the last time
I've seen you,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.239
you are now officially,
the term is,

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.174
you are an empty-nester.
-I know.

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:43.442
-Yeah.
-I am.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:44.810
-Both girls are
out of the house.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.078
-Yes, they are.

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:50.416
I have Iris, who's 19,
and she's now in college,

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:54.821
and then Maude, who is 24.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.055
Is she 25? No, she's --

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.323
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.892
She's 24?
-We'll correct it in post.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.959
-I think.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.293
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:04.097
And, um, yeah, I'm --

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:06.632
you know, I got pregnant --

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:08.101
So, yeah, she's 25.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.401
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:13.139
So, I got --
I got pregnant 25 years ago,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:17.543
and I basically have only
thought about them...

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:19.912
-Yeah.
-...and their interests

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:23.916
and their health and wellbeing,
and that's it.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.719
And haven't thought about myself
in 25 years.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.188
And now that they want nothing
to do with me, I'm like...

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.489
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:33.126
-I don't know what -- who I am.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.827
-Yeah, you maybe are a little --

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.562
you're, like, addicted to them,

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:39.298
and now you have to wean
yourself off, there, every day.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:42.602
-I think so, yeah.
I mean, I'm, like, lost.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:47.207
And people say, like,
"Do you have hobbies?

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:49.708
Or what are your interests?"

00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:52.411
And I don't have any.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.480
I know what Iris
is interested in

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.783
and what my Maude
is interested in,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.851
but i don't know.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.220
-And, okay, so, I -- I --

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.855
I've been talking
to a lot of people about this.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.890
-Trying to get advice.
-Yeah, yeah, like,

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.259
"What do I do
about this problem?"

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.728
And a lot of people are
telling me to try ayahuasca...

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:11.030
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.866
-...which is like, apparently,
you take ayahuasca,

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.101
which is like an amino acid.
-Okay.

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:19.405
-And, um, you meet God.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:23.576
-And God tells you
what your path should be.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.512
-Yes, it's like a supplement,
like a vitamin supplement.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.815
You get at it, like, GNC.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.050
No, but I've heard --
First of all,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.585
I'm gonna go out on a limb here

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:33.986
and say you're getting
a lot of advice

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:35.388
from parents
who live in Los Angeles.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.822
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:38.658
-I think I have.
-I think this is very much

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.560
empty-nester advice
from Hollywood.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.261
-i know, I know.

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:45.231
-'Cause it seems like
what I've heard about ayahuasca,

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.765
not having done it --
-You haven't done it?

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:49.335
-No, I haven't done it.
No interest, no interest.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.337
-Really?
-Absolutely not.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.272
-Okay.
-First of all,

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:56.842
it sounds very intense, right?
It's like sweat-lodgey and --

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.444
-Yeah, and vomiting.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:01.114
-Yeah, like
a 12- to 24-hour trip.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.015
Also, by the way,
I love His work.

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:04.984
I don't want to meet God.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.352
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.488
You know what I mean?
Like, I don't want to --

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:11.724
Also, I don't want to talk to
anybody who thinks they met him.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:15.027
-Right, I know.
-Know what I mean?

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.228
-Yes!
-Yeah!

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:18.664
-And what if he tells you,
like, do something

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:20.500
that you really
don't want to do?

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.168
Like, "Your path is this thing."

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.637
-Have you met people
who, like, lives are now taking,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.206
like, a sharp right turn because
that they did ayahuasca?

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:28.908
Now they're like, "Yeah,"
so now..."?

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:31.744
-No.
-"Now I'm wearing these shirts."

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:35.414
-No, those people don't seem...
-Yeah.

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:37.250
I think there's a lot of people
who are like, "I went,

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.851
and God said,
'You're doing great.'"

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.152
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:41.554
I think it's a lot of people
who are, like, already

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.222
feeling pretty good about
how they're doing, yeah.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:46.559
So don't do that.
-Don't do ayahuasca, okay?

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.996
-But also, like, I imagine,
as a mom,

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.498
you are, you know, a loving mom.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:53.633
You keep an eye on your kids.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:54.767
Did you have to, like,
at some point,

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.269
let go of that and let them...

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.770
Are you letting them
live their own lives?

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.538
Are you, like, not keeping tabs
on them

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:00.873
in the way you did
when they were in the house?

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.843
-Um, I gee --

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.077
I-I kind of...

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.712
Well, they...

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:08.147
Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:11.850
Since they moved out,
they stopped letting me

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.454
follow them on Find My Friends,
which is a tracking app.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:16.755
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:20.893
-But what they don't know is
that, um...

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.829
And we're not gonna tell them.
-No, of course not.

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.296
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:28.834
-...is that their Uber accounts
are connected to my credit card,

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.170
so every time
they go somewhere...

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.873
-Wow.
-...it alerts me.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.575
And which sounds really,
you know...

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:39.045
It's -- I know.
-Yeah.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.145
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.145 --> 00:04:42.615
But, um, okay, so, I, you know,

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.283
them being out of the house,
I get nervous

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:47.386
and I want to make sure that
they're home safe at night.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:50.823
And when I get the alert

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.793
that they're, like,
off to the bar or something,

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.328
I, um, you know, can't sleep.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:59.865
And so I sometimes
will text them, "Go home."

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:02.868
And -- And they're like...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:05.704
Like, "How does she know
I'm not at home?"

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:08.407
And they think I'm psychic.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:09.541
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:11.477
At least that --
At least they're

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.180
getting something from you
in this, sort of,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.149
because at least you're paying
for their Ubers, right?

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.783
-Right, yeah.
-You are being, like,

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.318
sort of a big-brother character
in their lives,

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:20.820
but at least, you know,
there's a little --

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.054
there's a little quid pro quo.

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:23.989
They're getting free rides.
-Free rides, yeah.

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:25.792
-And now, Maude,
who was here recently,

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.892
and it was so lovely
talking to her,

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:29.295
she is in "Euphoria,"
which is a show

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:30.396
that a lot of parents --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.598
Yes.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:37.903
This is a show
that panics parents,

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.972
because I think
a lot of parents watch that.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.840
And, you know, my kids
are younger than yours,

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.109
and when I see "Euphoria,"

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.610
I'm like, "Oh, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.113
I don't think you're ever
gonna go to school now."

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.447
-I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:50.182
-But you've had the benefit,
obviously,

00:05:50.182 --> 00:05:52.051
not only do you know Maude
but you've gotten to meet

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.753
some of the other people
in the show.

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:54.787
-Yes.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.289
-And that is, like, calming,
right?

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:59.124
-Well, it seems like --
I mean, the kids

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:01.260
are doing such crazy things
on the show,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.329
and then they'll come over
to the house

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:07.633
and they're, like, the nicest,
most polite kids

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:12.471
you've ever met,
and so, like, almost boring,

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:15.140
like, just up to nothing.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.475
I think I saw one of them

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.410
drink a White Claw once
or something.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.546
Like, just so sweet.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:23.616
And so they're just
really good actors.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:24.750
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.286
-Have you ever had
a couple glasses of wine

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.854
and just been honest and said,
"I thought

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.256
you were all gonna be
a lot more fun?"

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:31.790
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:34.126
-I'm the crazy one.
-You're like, "Aah!"

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:35.795
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:37.730
-"Let's go!"

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.732
You got to work --

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.167
We're gonna show a clip
when we come back,

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.970
but you got to work with Iris
on this film, "The Bubble,"

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.472
and your husband, Judd Apatow,
directed it.

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.407
So, you have three of you
there on set.

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:50.009
Is it -- I mean, that seems like
the best way

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:51.377
for a family
to spend time together,

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.678
but do you have boundaries
when you're on set together?

00:06:53.678 --> 00:06:54.980
-Well, he has boundaries,

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.115
and my daughter has boundaries
with me, obviously.

00:06:57.115 --> 00:06:58.484
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:01.921
-There's no, like,
hugging or chitchat.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.956
-This is what she asks of you.
-Yeah.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.858
She's like,
"Keep your distance,"

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:09.395
and you know, keeps it
really professional with me,

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:12.131
which is fine.

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.899
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:15.834
-I mean, she's --

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.838
I mean, I appreciate
what she's doing.

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:21.206
I can't imagine it's like, easy,
but you have to, like, go,

00:07:21.206 --> 00:07:22.908
"Well, professionally,
she's probably right."

00:07:22.908 --> 00:07:25.878
-Yeah, she wants me to back off,
'cause she wants to do her work.

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:28.347
-You know, I'm lucky enough,
Judd will be here tomorrow,

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.548
and I can obviously
ask him this.

00:07:29.548 --> 00:07:31.284
Does he feel comfortable
directing her?

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:32.484
I mean...

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:36.688
-I think that he is
a little bit, um,

00:07:36.688 --> 00:07:39.058
you know --
he's very --

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:43.162
that's his one area to be, like,
bossy and controlling with us,

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:45.697
because they rule him at home.

00:07:45.697 --> 00:07:48.133
-Oh, right.
-So, he's at work.

00:07:48.133 --> 00:07:49.635
He gets a little, you know --

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:51.670
he gets to, like, you know,
speak up.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.172
-Oh, that's nice.

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:54.674
So it's cathartic for him,
I Imagine,

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:56.208
growing up in
a house full of women.

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:57.977
For him to finally be able to,
like, say "Cut"

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:59.645
when you're talking
must be so nice.

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:01.747
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:03.149
-Exactly.

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:05.518
-I have more questions
about "The Bubble."

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:07.353
We'll be right back
with more from Leslie Mann.

